@HD	VN:1.6	SO:unsorted	GO:query
@SQ	SN:chr1	LN:240
@SQ	SN:chr2	LN:240
@CO	03-methyl-hic-chimera. All molecules are bisulfite-converted on the molecule strand: every C not followed by G reads as T in both mates.
@CO	hic_sup_overlap: ligation product chr1:41-100(+) | chr2:101-140(+), L=100. R1 (80 bp) = primary chr1:41-100 60M20S + supplementary chr2:101-120 60H20M (MAPQ 40).
@CO	hic_sup_overlap: R2 (35 bp) = single reverse record chr2:106-140. True overlap f[65,80) = chr2:106-120, all on R1's SUPPLEMENTARY. R1 and R2 primaries are on different contigs.
@CO	hic_junction_overlap: same molecule, R2 is 50 bp and split: primary chr2:101-140 10S40M (rev), supplementary chr1:91-100 10M40H (rev, MAPQ 10). Overlap f[50,80) spans the ligation junction: chr1:91-100 + chr2:101-120.
@CO	hic_inverted: chr1:41-100(+) | chr2:101-140 entered against the reference. R1 supplementary is reverse on chr2:121-140, R2 is forward on chr2:101-135. Overlap f[65,80) = chr2:121-135.
@CO	colinear_control: ordinary 60 bp fragment chr1:141-200, reads 40/40, overlap chr1:161-180. Used to show samtools mpileup's own overlap detection working on a colinear pair.
